h4. Tags

A tag is a single word or a phrase joined with underscores that says something true about the post. Tags are what search matches, so a post is only as findable as its tags are complete.

h4. Categories

* [b]General[/b] -- what is in the image: 1girl, sword, outdoors.
* [b]Character[/b] -- who is in it.
* [b]Copyright[/b] -- what it is from.
* [b]Artist[/b] -- who made it. On this site the artist tag is usually the poster's own name or the board it came from.
* [b]Meta[/b] -- facts about the file rather than the picture: highres, animated, translated.

Each category has its own colour wherever tags are shown, and that colour never changes to mean anything else.

h4. Where the tags come from

Nearly every tag here was written by a tagger, not a person. Two models run on every image and each pill on a post says which -- see [[help:autotags]]. You can add and remove tags on any post you can see; a tag you add is marked as yours.

h4. Tags that are not there

Some tags have been removed from the vocabulary of this site: they do not appear in listings, in autocomplete, or on posts, for anyone. Posts that carried them are handled separately. See [[help:blacklists]].

h4. Keeping the vocabulary tidy

* [[help:tag_aliases]] -- one spelling wins.
* [[help:tag_implications]] -- one tag brings another with it.
* [[help:bulk_update_requests]] -- proposing either.
* [[help:deprecation_notice]] -- tags that can no longer be added.
